# Cloudflare Workers parses this file and applies it to static assets before the Worker
# runs (the Worker only serves /api/subscribe). Two rules of the format matter:
#   - the first matching line wins, so order counts;
#   - all static rules must come before any wildcard rule.
# It is inert under `astro dev` and `astro build`, so changes here can only be tested on
# the deployed site. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/

# --- Bio links -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The short URLs that go in the Instagram, TikTok and YouTube bios. They are short
# because they are typed and read aloud, and they carry the utm tags so the traffic from
# each platform can be told apart. 302, not 301: which platform points where will change,
# and a 301 would be cached in readers' browsers for a long time.
#
# NOTE: Cloudflare Web Analytics, which this site uses, does not log query strings, so
# these utm tags produce no separate numbers there today. They are what any analytics
# tool added later will read. See docs/links-page.md.

/ig   /links/?utm_source=instagram&utm_medium=bio   302
/tt   /links/?utm_source=tiktok&utm_medium=bio      302
/yt   /links/?utm_source=youtube&utm_medium=bio     302

# --- Old /articles/ URLs, kept working --------------------------------------------
#
# The section was renamed Articles -> Essays on 2026-11-23 and the URLs moved with it.
# The first essay was published that same day, so links to /articles/... are already out
# and cannot be edited after the fact. These rules make them land on the right page.
# Never delete them.

/articles     /essays/        301
/articles/    /essays/        301
/articles/*   /essays/:splat  301
